==English==
{{was wotd|2024|November|8}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sed-}}
From {{m|en|set|pos=verb}} + {{m|en|about|pos=adverb, preposition}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|subentry=to set about|subpos=phrasal v|subid=4802840598|entry=set|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=6993814720|date=September 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=phrasal v}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/sɛt‿əˈbaʊt/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|aʊt|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|set<,,set> about}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Used with the {{glossary|adverb}} sense of ''about''.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|chiefly|Northern England}} To [[circulate]] or [[spread#Verb|spread]] ([[news#Noun|news]], a [[rumor#Noun|rumour]], etc.)
##* {{RQ:Burnet History|volume=I|page=663|passage=For ſome vveeks before it {{quote-gloss|Parliament}} met there vvas ſuch a number of Refugees coming over every day, vvho '''ſet about''' a moſt diſmal recital of the perſecution in ''France'', and that in ſo many inſtances that vvere crying and odious, {{...}}}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Used with the {{glossary|preposition}} sense of ''about''.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}}
### {{lb|en|archaic}} To [[plant#Verb|plant]] [[tree#Noun|trees]] or other [[vegetation]] around (a [[place#Noun|place]]).
###* {{RQ:Evelyn Diary|year=1646|month=March|volume=I|page=218|passage=[I]ndeede the whole island is a mount ascended by several terraces and walks all '''set about''' with orange and citron trees.}}
### {{lb|en|passive voice|archaic}} To [[encircle]] or [[surround#Verb|surround]] (something) with other [[thing]]s.
###* {{RQ:Evelyn Diary|entrydate=15 February 1645|volume=I|page=152|passage=Ascending the hill we came to St. Sabina, an ancient fabric, formerly sacred to [[w:Diana (mythology)|Diana]]; there in a Chapel is an admirable picture, the work of Livia Fontana, '''set about''' with columns of alabaster, {{...}}}}
### {{lb|en|UK|informal}} To [[attack#Verb|attack]] (someone); to [[set upon]].
###: {{synonyms|en|begin upon}}
###: {{ux|en|Two youths '''set about''' him.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[start#Verb|start]] [[do#Verb|doing]] or to [[devote#Verb|devote]] oneself to some [[task#Noun|task]]; to set upon.
##: {{synonyms|en|begin upon|[[embark]] on|take in hand}}
##: {{ux|en|He '''set about''' designing his homepage.}}
##* {{RQ:Evelyn Diary|entrydate=20 February 1666|volume=I|page=384|passage=To y{{sup|e}} Commiss{{sup|rs}} of the Navy, who having seene the project of the Infirmary, encourag'd the work, and were very earnest it should be '''set about''' immediately; {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Burnet History|volume=I|page=3|passage=I look on the perfecting of this vvork, and the carrying it on thro' the remaining part of my life, as the greateſt ſervice I can do to God and to the vvorld; and therefore I '''ſet about''' it vvith great care and caution.}}
##* {{RQ:Scott Tales of My Landlord 3|volume=II|chapter=XII|page=307|passage=Let every man and woman here '''set about''' their ain business, as if there was nae sic thing as marquis or master, duke or drake, laird or lord, in this world.}}
##* {{RQ:Ruskin Sesame and Lilies|page=5|passage=[T]his essential education might be more easily got, or given, than they fancy, if they '''set about''' it in the right way; while it is for no price, and by no favour, to be got, if they '''set about''' it in the wrong.}}
##* {{RQ:Doyle Micah Clarke|chapter=Of the Swordsman with the Brown Jacket|page=313|passage="Then we had best '''set about''' our part of the contract," said Hector Marot.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1963|month=June|title=News and Comment: Road–rail Co-operation|journal=w:Modern Railways|location=Shepperton, Surrey|publisher=w:Ian Allan Publishing|page=362|issn=0026-8356|oclc=884584817|passage=No time has been lost in '''setting about''' the implementation of non-controversial [[w:Richard Beeching|{{quote-gloss|Richard}} Beeching]] proposals.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|date=22 March 2012|author=Scott Tobias|title=[[w:The Hunger Games (film)|The Hunger Games]]|work=w:The A.V. Club|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221025151424/https://www.avclub.com/the-hunger-games-1798172070|passage=A book is a book and a movie is a movie, and whenever the latter merely '''sets about''' illustrating the former, it's a failure of adaptation, to say nothing of imagination.}}

